EF AI Workspace (#204): sidebar v4, owner-approved 2026-10-25 (Concept 2 «الشريط واللوحة»: «اعتمد المفهوم 2 ونفذه بدقة»).
The v3 column left the chat history about 30% of its height (15% with «More» open); the history now has a panel of its
own beside a rail, as upstream's unified sidebar (a labelled rail beside a panel) already arranges it.

- Rail (UnifiedSidebar/ExpandedPanel.tsx, constants.ts: 76 px), always shown on the desktop: the «Baseer» icon, «New
  chat», «Chats» (opens and closes the chats panel, pressed while it shows them; a tool in the panel gives way to the
  chats), a line, Projects, Skills and Documents (pages, the open one marked), «More» (EfMoreMenu.tsx: memory,
  bookmarks, ready commands; for admins the marketplace, the builder and the parameters under «Admins only»), the
  account. It keeps the hidden shortcut targets.
- Chats panel (UnifiedSidebar/EfChatsPanel.tsx, replaces EfSidebarColumn.tsx; Sidebar.tsx, UnifiedSidebar.tsx): beside
  the rail at full height, 300 px and resizable (the handle at its inner edge, the pointer and arrows following the page
  direction). Header «Chats» with upstream's sort and filter menu (ChatFilterMenu) and the collapse control; the chat
  search; the chips «All / Pinned / Project» (EfChatChips.tsx, efChatScope.ts: «Pinned» alone, or one project's chats
  or those of none, filtered by the server's `projectId`, its pinned chats first); the history. The list's own «Chats»
  heading steps aside (Conversations.tsx `hideHeader`, `emptyLabel`; ConversationsSection.tsx). Pages never replace the
  panel; the admin chat-bound tools keep it with «Back to chats».
- Phone: the drawer is the chats screen: header (icon, «Chats», sort and filter, account, close), search, chips,
  history, a floating «New chat», and a tab bar (Chats, Projects, Skills, Documents, More) whose tabs close the drawer
  and open their page; each tab takes its name's width so «المستندات» and «Documents» stay whole on a 360 px phone.
- Tests: ExpandedPanel.spec (the rail and «Chats»), ConversationsSection.spec (the chips), drawerPaint.spec (the panel).

